        {
          name: 'The watch\'s muster hall',
          one_liner: 'The room where the city\'s lanterns line up before dusk.',
          subject: 'a watch\'s muster hall',
          detail:
            'A long bench, a brass whistle, and a tall narrow door that everyone walks through twice. The first time is to be recognized. The second is to be assigned. The lantern you carry out is the one you bring back.',
          tags: ['watch', 'muster'],
        },
        {
          name: 'The paupers\' dormitory',
          one_liner: 'A long floor where strangers learn to sleep without noise.',
          subject: 'a city paupers\' dormitory',
          detail:
            'Straw mats in rows, a single iron stove, and a register the attendant reads by lamplight. Nobody is turned away at night. In the morning, those who can work are pointed toward the bureau that knows them by name.',
          tags: ['dormitory', 'paupers'],
        },
      ],
    },
    {
      kind: 'monument',
      entries: [
        {
          name: 'The bell tower',
          one_liner: 'A tall wooden tower whose voice the whole city hears.',
          subject: 'a city bell tower',
          detail:
            'The bell is not rung for the hours. It is rung for the occasions: a magistrate takes office, a fire is out, a flood recedes, a funeral passes. The tower\'s wood is dark with soot that no one has scrubbed for a hundred years.',
          tags: ['tower', 'bell'],
        },
        {
          name: 'The south gate',
          one_liner: 'The wide gate every traveler walks through first.',
          subject: 'a city south gate',
          detail:
            'The road worn into a polished trough by a thousand incoming feet. Two wooden doors, one always open in daylight, with guards who check identities more by face than by paper. The road is wide because the gate is generous.',
          tags: ['gate', 'south'],
        },
        {
          name: 'The dry river\'s stone arches',
          one_liner: 'A bridge that crosses a river that has not come in years.',
          subject: 'a dry-river stone bridge',
          detail:
            'Five low arches under a road of packed earth. The riverbed is dry for most summers, a thin rivulet in autumn, a torrent for a week each spring. The old arches remember a year the river came twice, and so does the wall beside them.',
          tags: ['arches', 'dry'],
        },
        {
          name: 'The founder\'s stela',
          one_liner: 'A tall stone with a name the city can\'t quite read.',
          subject: 'a founder\'s stela',
          detail:
